  "highlights": [
    "versioned acceptance packs @1 for runtime, coding, research, deployment, data-pipeline and Harness release workflows",
    "TrustedCheckRegistry provides a fingerprintable deployment-owned allow-list so contracts reference reviewed check ids instead of arbitrary command strings",
    "new deterministic artifact.exists, artifact.nonempty, runtime.recovery-clean, evidence.no-contradictions and external.resource-exists verifier primitives",
    "goal outcome adapter supports observe mode for would-reject calibration and enforce mode for fail-closed completion",
    "labeled verifier benchmark computes false-acceptance rate (FAR), false-rejection rate (FRR), latency, verifier runs, evidence volume and repair rounds",
    "hardening experiment layer can summarize verification observations and compare pack versions by FAR/FRR deltas",
    "release-v1 dogfooding configuration defines trusted check ids, observe-mode rollout and a zero-FAR promotion policy",
    "root check/release chains include v0.10 source and labeled verifier qualification"
  ],
  "remaining_work": [
    "grow each pack benchmark from synthetic qualification fixtures to at least 50 labeled real-world valid/invalid cases before enforce-mode promotion",
    "bind first-party trusted check ids to dependency-backed CI implementations for tests, typecheck, security, packaging, deployment and research evidence quality",
    "persist pack calibration runs and FAR/FRR history as release artifacts and compare pack versions on identical corpora",
    "protect acceptance fixtures/golden outputs from worker mutation with explicit filesystem/tool authority enforcement",
    "dogfood release@1 in enforce mode only after observe-mode corpus demonstrates acceptable false-rejection rate with zero false acceptance",
    "run dependency-backed full monorepo CI and verified-success paired experiments on real coding tasks"
  ],
